(1574, 'house', '/haʊs/', 'noun', '{"zh-TW":["【主要意義-名詞】房子；住宅","【次要意義-動詞】容納；收藏；為……提供住所","【次要意義-名詞】議院；劇院；公司"],"en":["[primary - noun] a building for people to live in","[secondary - verb] to provide accommodation or storage space for something","[secondary - noun] a legislative assembly; a theater; a business firm"]}', NULL, 'house a collection / house equipment / the House of Representatives / in-house', '[{"en":"The new facility houses the company''s entire research and development team.","zh-TW":"新設施容納了公司整個研發團隊。"},{"en":"The museum houses over 10,000 works of art from around the world.","zh-TW":"博物館收藏了來自世界各地的逾萬件藝術品。"},{"en":"The server room houses all the critical data infrastructure.","zh-TW":"伺服器機房容納了所有關鍵的資料基礎設施。"}]', '{"noun":"housing, household","adjective":"in-house"}', '動詞 house（發音 /haʊz/）意為「容納/收藏」，常見於 TOEIC 描述設施、建築或機構功能的閱讀文章，考生易誤讀為名詞。', 2, 1574, NULL),
